---
title: Blender Gluten Free Pumpkin Muffins
servings: 12
cuisine: american
main_protein: dairy
prep_time: "20 minutes"
cook_time: "18 minutes"
tags:
  - breakfast
  - pumpkin
  - oats
  - muffins
source: https://krollskorner.com/recipes/desserts/flourless-pumpkin-muffin-bites/
image: ../obsidian/attachments/blender-gluten-free-pumpkin-muffins.jpg
leftover_portions: 8
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 425°F
  - Coat muffin tin with non-stick spray
  - Measure out spices
  - Set aside 0.25 cup chocolate chips for topping
---
Heat #oven{} to 425°F and coat #muffin tin{} with non-stick spray.

Using a #food processor{} or blender, pulse @old-fashioned rolled oats{2%cups} for approximately ~{15%seconds} until partially ground.

Add remaining ingredients (@greek yogurt{1%cup}, @canned pumpkin{1%cup}, @egg{2}, @vegetable oil{0.25%cup} or melted coconut oil, @honey{2%tbsp}, @baking powder{2%tsp}, @baking soda{0.5%tsp}, @cinnamon{1%tsp}, @nutmeg{0.5%tsp}, @pumpkin spice{0.5%tsp}, @salt{0.5%tsp}, @turmeric{0.125%tsp} and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}) except pepitas and chocolate chips. Blend until smooth. Fold in 3/4 cup of the @dark chocolate chips{1%cup}, reserving remainder for topping.

Distribute batter into prepared muffin cups, filling three-quarters full. Top with @pepitas{} (optional) and remaining chocolate chips.

Bake ~{15%minutes} until a toothpick inserted in center comes out clean. Cool briefly before serving.
